    "summary": "High‑energy Europe ’72 with epic Truckin’>Other One suite and tight Lovelight",
    "blurb": "The Frankfurt show delivers a tour‑defining Truckin' → The Other One jam, backed by a crisp Turn On Your Lovelight. Jerry’s solos sparkle throughout, while Phil provides thematic bass lines that lift the second set. Strong first‑set moments like Good Lovin’ and Jack Straw round out an inspired performance.",
    "review": "April 26, 1972 at Frankfurt's Jahrhundert Halle captures the Dead in top form during their legendary Europe ’72 run. The band launches into a marathon first set that weaves through classics—Bertha, China Cat Sunflower > I Know You Rider, Jack Straw and an exuberant Good Lovin’—setting a bright, flowing mood that carries straight into a second‑set masterpiece. A blistering Truckin' segues seamlessly into an expansive Other One where Jerry Garcia shreds with magical intensity, his lead lines soaring over Phil Lesh’s thematic bass “bombs.” The climax rolls into a soulful Turn On Your Lovelight, showcasing vocal power from Bob and tight keyboard textures from Keith, before the rhythm section—Bill Kreutzmann’s propulsive drums and the rest of the crew—drives the groove into a jubilant Sugar Magnolia. Across all four soundboard sources the audio is crystal‑clear, making this one of the most accessible and exhilarating recordings of the era.",
